# PowerShell backtick line-continuations in the Windows workflows are broken by
# CRLF: a backtick before CR escapes the CR, not the newline, so the continuation
# dies with "Missing expression after unary operator". Force LF for workflow YAML.
.github/workflows/*.yml text eol=lf

# Shell scripts must stay LF in the working tree on EVERY platform, mirroring
# the rule ContainerHub already carries. They are run by bash inside Linux
# containers, and on a Windows host this repo is bind-mounted into one - the
# documented Rancher Desktop workflow. Without this, core.autocrlf=true gives
# them CRLF and bash dies on the trailing \r with errors that name the wrong
# culprit: "set: pipefail\r: invalid option name", "$'\r': command not found".
# Verified 2026-08-07: this is exactly how a local Rancher build failed.
*.sh text eol=lf
*.bash text eol=lf
